1
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,543
[♪ adventurous music plays]

2
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:49,960
[Lo'ak] Come on, Bro.

3
00:00:51,043 --> 00:00:52,043
[laughs]

4
00:00:53,085 --> 00:00:56,001
Whoo! Whoo, whoo, whoo!

5
00:00:56,668 --> 00:00:57,585
[chuckles]

6
00:01:05,126 --> 00:01:06,751
Whoo! [chuckles]

7
00:01:07,501 --> 00:01:08,876
[Lo'ak ululates]

8
00:01:10,835 --> 00:01:12,125
Whoo!

9
00:01:12,126 --> 00:01:13,959
Whoa. Whoa.

10
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:15,042
Hey, watch it.

11
00:01:15,043 --> 00:01:16,875
You were in my way, Bro.

12
00:01:16,876 --> 00:01:18,376
Oh, okay.

13
00:01:19,043 --> 00:01:21,168
- [Lo'ak] Whoo--
- [shrieks]

14
00:01:24,418 --> 00:01:25,626
Whoo!

15
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:27,793
[grunts]

16
00:01:29,626 --> 00:01:30,835
Whoo!

17
00:01:32,501 --> 00:01:34,084
Whoo!

18
00:01:34,085 --> 00:01:35,542
[chuckles] Is that
all you got?

19
00:01:35,543 --> 00:01:37,668
You want to go faster, huh?

20
00:01:45,626 --> 00:01:47,710
[chuckles] Whoo-hoo!

21
00:01:51,126 --> 00:01:54,167
- [both panting]
- [ikran squawk]

22
00:01:54,168 --> 00:01:55,501
That was cool, Bro.

23
00:01:56,168 --> 00:01:57,751
[chuckles] <i>Skxawng</i>, let go.

24
00:02:01,043 --> 00:02:02,375
It was cool riding
with you, Bro.

25
00:02:02,376 --> 00:02:03,668
High four.

26
00:02:04,251 --> 00:02:05,334
[sighs]

27
00:02:05,335 --> 00:02:06,835
- [scoffs]
- [chuckles]

28
00:02:09,710 --> 00:02:12,000
[sighs]

29
00:02:12,001 --> 00:02:13,668
All right,
I got to get back, Bro.

30
00:02:14,501 --> 00:02:15,751
Little Brother,

31
00:02:16,376 --> 00:02:18,376
tell me one thing
before you go.

32
00:02:21,001 --> 00:02:22,210
How did I die?

33
00:02:28,876 --> 00:02:30,335
You got shot.

34
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:34,043
We could have escaped, but I
made us go back for Spider.

35
00:02:35,251 --> 00:02:36,585
Then we had to go back.

36
00:02:37,376 --> 00:02:38,459
That's not your fault.

37
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:39,626
Tell that to Dad.

38
00:02:40,210 --> 00:02:42,293
We weren't even supposed
to be out there.

39
00:02:43,710 --> 00:02:46,625
I got us caught
because I disobeyed orders.

40
00:02:46,626 --> 00:02:48,418
That's just you, Little Bro.

41
00:02:58,835 --> 00:03:00,210
I love you, Brother.

42
00:03:00,835 --> 00:03:01,835
<i>Skxawng.</i>

43
00:03:07,751 --> 00:03:09,335
[Lo'ak] <i>I killed my brother.</i>

44
00:03:10,210 --> 00:03:11,418
<i>No matter what happens,</i>

45
00:03:12,168 --> 00:03:15,543
<i>I have to live with that
for the rest of my life.</i>

46
00:03:44,710 --> 00:03:47,668
[panting]

47
00:03:54,043 --> 00:03:55,126
I wish I could do it.

48
00:03:55,668 --> 00:03:57,710
No, I wish I could do it.

49
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:02,084
If I have another
stupid seizure underwater...

50
00:04:02,085 --> 00:04:03,167
Yeah,

51
00:04:03,168 --> 00:04:05,000
you'd be me
without a mask.

52
00:04:05,001 --> 00:04:07,334
[imitates choking]

53
00:04:07,335 --> 00:04:08,750
- Uh, let's test that.
- Hey, hey.

54
00:04:08,751 --> 00:04:10,292
- Watch it.
- See what happens.

55
00:04:10,293 --> 00:04:11,418
Hey, watch the stitches.

56
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:14,417
Uh-huh. Yeah,
how do you like that, huh?

57
00:04:14,418 --> 00:04:15,418
- No! Ow! [shrieks]
- [laughs]

58
00:04:21,043 --> 00:04:23,793
[♪ Neytiri singing in Na'vi]

59
00:04:38,293 --> 00:04:39,959
[Lo'ak] <i>The fire of hate</i>

60
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:41,835
<i>leaves only
the ash of grief.</i>

61
00:04:43,793 --> 00:04:45,209
<i>My mother mourned</i>

62
00:04:45,210 --> 00:04:46,293
<i>the ancient way,</i>

63
00:04:46,835 --> 00:04:49,376
<i>singing her son's life
during the daily eclipse.</i>

64
00:04:51,293 --> 00:04:53,168
<i>Because the light
always returns.</i>

65
00:04:59,876 --> 00:05:00,793
[singing fades]

66
00:05:02,710 --> 00:05:03,835
[Lo'ak] <i>There's the</i> Na'vi <i>way,</i>

67
00:05:04,835 --> 00:05:06,335
<i>and then there's
my dad's way.</i>

68
00:05:07,043 --> 00:05:09,418
<i>Say nothing.
Keep busy.</i>

69
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:14,126
[breathes heavily]

70
00:05:24,626 --> 00:05:25,626
[ilu shrieks]

71
00:05:28,251 --> 00:05:30,501
[Lo'ak] <i>The Reef People say
the sea washes you clean.</i>

72
00:05:32,001 --> 00:05:33,584
<i>Washes away your sins.</i>

73
00:05:33,585 --> 00:05:34,751
[ilu squeaks]

74
00:06:10,543 --> 00:06:11,543
What do you got?

75
00:06:13,376 --> 00:06:14,792
You're supposed
to be collecting guns.

76
00:06:14,793 --> 00:06:16,251
That thing's useless.

77
00:06:16,835 --> 00:06:17,960
Focus, boy.

78
00:06:23,710 --> 00:06:25,335
Don't let your mother
see that.

79
00:06:34,376 --> 00:06:35,375
Hey, excuse me.

80
00:06:35,376 --> 00:06:36,917
- Sorry. [laughs]
- Excuse me.

81
00:06:36,918 --> 00:06:38,043
- Tuk.
- [Tuk] Sorry.

82
00:06:45,126 --> 00:06:46,126
Bro.

83
00:06:47,751 --> 00:06:49,001
Ah, sick.

84
00:06:50,418 --> 00:06:51,418
What is this?

85
00:06:52,668 --> 00:06:53,668
Tsireya?

86
00:06:55,168 --> 00:06:56,501
What are you doing?

87
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:01,417
This is an AR, all right?

88
00:07:01,418 --> 00:07:03,542
This is the mag.
It's where the bullets are.

89
00:07:03,543 --> 00:07:04,710
Empty.

90
00:07:05,626 --> 00:07:06,626
Slap it.

91
00:07:07,585 --> 00:07:08,625
Rack it.

92
00:07:08,626 --> 00:07:10,000
And then, boom,

93
00:07:10,001 --> 00:07:11,125
you can just spray.

94
00:07:11,126 --> 00:07:13,375
[chuckles] You can kill
a lot of Sky People with this.

95
00:07:13,376 --> 00:07:15,542
See? Ceramic action.

96
00:07:15,543 --> 00:07:17,667
You clean 'em and oil 'em,
be as good as new.

97
00:07:17,668 --> 00:07:19,750
This is not the <i>Na'vi</i> way,

98
00:07:19,751 --> 00:07:20,959
<i>Jakesully</i>.

99
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:23,125
Weapons of metal
are forbidden.

100
00:07:23,126 --> 00:07:24,209
You know this.

101
00:07:24,210 --> 00:07:25,292
To touch them

102
00:07:25,293 --> 00:07:26,710
poisons the heart.

103
00:07:27,210 --> 00:07:28,292
Eywa

104
00:07:28,293 --> 00:07:29,376
will provide.

105
00:07:30,001 --> 00:07:31,876
[sighs] Right.

106
00:07:32,918 --> 00:07:35,292
The mourning period
is not even over.

107
00:07:35,293 --> 00:07:36,209
Tuk.

108
00:07:36,210 --> 00:07:37,667
[Ronal] You should be
with your family,

109
00:07:37,668 --> 00:07:39,459
not gathering these things.

110
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:41,042
Your woman

111
00:07:41,043 --> 00:07:42,168
needs you.

112
00:07:44,210 --> 00:07:47,210
My son lies with the ancestors
in the reef.

113
00:07:48,085 --> 00:07:49,709
This is our home.

114
00:07:49,710 --> 00:07:51,667
I said I would stand and fight,

115
00:07:51,668 --> 00:07:54,459
but I can't fight gunships
with spears.

116
00:07:54,460 --> 00:07:56,375
We sank the demon ship.

117
00:07:56,376 --> 00:07:58,126
The pink skins fear us now.

118
00:07:59,751 --> 00:08:01,792
Yeah? We got lucky.

119
00:08:01,793 --> 00:08:03,251
And they got many more ships.

120
00:08:04,043 --> 00:08:05,460
Least we got these.

121
00:08:06,668 --> 00:08:09,001
We are grateful you
stand with us, <i>Jakesully</i>.

122
00:08:09,668 --> 00:08:11,084
It is not guns we need.

123
00:08:11,085 --> 00:08:12,501
It is Rider of Last Shadow.

124
00:08:14,293 --> 00:08:16,000
Ride great <i>toruk</i>

125
00:08:16,001 --> 00:08:18,043
as you did before.

126
00:08:18,710 --> 00:08:22,709
[inhales deeply]
When you ride the beast,

127
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:24,043
you become the beast.

128
00:08:25,335 --> 00:08:27,418
And the more blood,
the better.

129
00:08:29,085 --> 00:08:31,042
I will not become

130
00:08:31,043 --> 00:08:33,001
<i>Toruk Makto</i> again.

131
00:08:34,043 --> 00:08:35,251
<i>Jakesully</i>,

132
00:08:36,210 --> 00:08:38,335
you are always <i>Toruk Makto.</i>

133
00:08:39,501 --> 00:08:41,543
Come. Rotxo.

134
00:08:47,210 --> 00:08:48,251
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

135
00:08:48,876 --> 00:08:50,167
[Scoresby] Yeah, we can
hear you loud and clear.

136
00:08:50,168 --> 00:08:51,168
Go on, Doc.

137
00:08:52,085 --> 00:08:55,417
<i>So, uh, we've been through
the wreck, inside and out.</i>

138
00:08:55,418 --> 00:08:58,585
<i>Uh, we've searched to about
a 200-meter radius around it.</i>

139
00:08:59,126 --> 00:09:00,709
<i>We didn't find
any</i> Na'vi <i>bodies.</i>

140
00:09:00,710 --> 00:09:03,792
<i>Just crew or...
what's left of 'em.</i>

141
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:06,167
Well, keep looking, Doctor.

142
00:09:06,168 --> 00:09:08,459
- Expand the search radius.
- [Dr. Garvin] <i>Roger that.</i>

143
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:09,375
<i>Of note though,</i>

144
00:09:09,376 --> 00:09:11,376
<i>I did find an interesting
new algae.</i>

145
00:09:13,168 --> 00:09:14,667
<i>Hello? Can you hear me?</i>

146
00:09:14,668 --> 00:09:16,959
- Sully is still out there.
- [Ardmore] We don't know that.

147
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:19,125
Scavengers could have
carried off the bodies.

148
00:09:19,126 --> 00:09:21,667
Nope. He made it out.

149
00:09:21,668 --> 00:09:25,167
And he's in this area.
Down to a handful of villages.

150
00:09:25,168 --> 00:09:26,709
You just give me a ship
and I'll--

151
00:09:26,710 --> 00:09:27,875
I gave you a ship.

152
00:09:27,876 --> 00:09:29,626
It's right there,
on the bottom.

153
00:09:30,376 --> 00:09:31,793
Yeah. Along with my crew.

154
00:09:32,626 --> 00:09:33,626
All dead.

155
00:09:34,626 --> 00:09:36,459
You brought me out here,

156
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:38,584
twenty-six trillion miles,

157
00:09:38,585 --> 00:09:40,292
for a single mission,

158
00:09:40,293 --> 00:09:41,875
a kinetic hard kill op

159
00:09:41,876 --> 00:09:43,876
against one guy.

160
00:09:44,418 --> 00:09:46,335
I ain't backing off.

161
00:09:50,001 --> 00:09:52,085
[Dr. Garvin]
<i>Are we still connected? Hello?</i>

162
00:09:53,210 --> 00:09:54,793
<i>Do they have me on mute?</i>

163
00:10:01,710 --> 00:10:04,085
The spirit of my ancestors
is in this bow.

164
00:10:06,543 --> 00:10:07,751
It was our strength.

165
00:10:10,918 --> 00:10:13,376
I can help you
fix it, Lo'ak.

166
00:10:15,085 --> 00:10:16,085
No!

167
00:10:17,335 --> 00:10:18,418
It's ruined!

168
00:10:19,626 --> 00:10:21,626
[Lo'ak] <i>Everything I touch
gets ruined.</i>

169
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:28,251
<i>They never talked about it.</i>

170
00:10:30,293 --> 00:10:31,751
<i>But it was there
in the room.</i>

171
00:10:32,376 --> 00:10:34,334
<i>Like a crouching thanator.</i>

172
00:10:34,335 --> 00:10:35,585
[sighs]

173
00:10:37,501 --> 00:10:39,626
I know you will never
give up your bow.

174
00:10:41,626 --> 00:10:42,626
So...

175
00:10:47,501 --> 00:10:49,251
Just don't be close
when it hits.

176
00:10:52,751 --> 00:10:54,792
[sighs]

177
00:10:54,793 --> 00:10:57,210
[breathing shakily]

178
00:11:08,043 --> 00:11:10,210
So, you agree with Ronal?

179
00:11:14,001 --> 00:11:15,959
I will never speak against
my husband

180
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:17,460
in front of that woman.

181
00:11:20,085 --> 00:11:21,293
Look, I'm a marine.

182
00:11:23,251 --> 00:11:25,126
I'm not taking a knife
to a gunfight.

183
00:11:27,335 --> 00:11:28,460
Or a prayer. [scoffs]

184
00:11:31,126 --> 00:11:32,835
So, what am I
supposed to do?

185
00:11:33,918 --> 00:11:36,376
I can't run.
I can't fight.

186
00:11:36,876 --> 00:11:37,876
Oh, that's right.

187
00:11:38,543 --> 00:11:41,625
Eywa will provide. Yeah?
So, where was Eywa?

188
00:11:41,626 --> 00:11:43,417
Where was Eywa
when our son--

189
00:11:43,418 --> 00:11:44,418
Jake!

190
00:11:47,085 --> 00:11:49,626
I'm in this place
where I have nothing.

191
00:11:50,835 --> 00:11:53,460
Not my people,
not my forest.

192
00:11:54,918 --> 00:11:56,835
Even my father's bow
is gone.

193
00:11:59,835 --> 00:12:00,960
All I have...

194
00:12:02,251 --> 00:12:03,501
is my faith

195
00:12:04,335 --> 00:12:06,751
that this is
the Great Mother's plan.

196
00:12:07,251 --> 00:12:09,709
[breathing shakily]

197
00:12:09,710 --> 00:12:11,293
You have this family.

198
00:12:25,501 --> 00:12:26,835
And you have me.

199
00:12:29,126 --> 00:12:31,085
And I love you so much.

200
00:12:35,585 --> 00:12:38,001
[sobs]

201
00:12:40,710 --> 00:12:44,084
[chittering]

202
00:12:44,085 --> 00:12:45,834
[♪ adventurous music plays]

203
00:12:45,835 --> 00:12:46,960
[bellows]

204
00:12:52,876 --> 00:12:54,584
[whistles]

205
00:12:54,585 --> 00:12:56,709
Yeah, Payakan,
you're the man!

206
00:12:56,710 --> 00:12:59,043
[rumbles]

207
00:13:03,501 --> 00:13:05,543
[tulkun vocalizing]

208
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:24,960
Whoa. Bro, Bro.

209
00:13:25,543 --> 00:13:26,543
[exclaims]

210
00:13:28,210 --> 00:13:30,710
This is sick! [laughs]

211
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:35,001
- Whoo! Whoo!
- Whoo-hoo!

212
00:13:37,001 --> 00:13:38,501
Whoo!

213
00:13:41,168 --> 00:13:43,210
- [laughs]
- [screams]

214
00:13:45,293 --> 00:13:47,043
- Whoo! [laughs]
- Bro, come on! Go, go, go, go!

215
00:13:47,751 --> 00:13:49,543
- Oh, sh...
- Yeah!

216
00:13:54,668 --> 00:13:56,334
That was insane, cuz.

217
00:13:56,335 --> 00:13:57,501
I know, right, Bro?

218
00:13:58,543 --> 00:13:59,667
[Tsireya laughs]

219
00:13:59,668 --> 00:14:00,835
I thought you were dead.

220
00:14:01,585 --> 00:14:03,710
[both imitate splash, laugh]

221
00:14:04,751 --> 00:14:07,500
It sucks that Payakan
is still an outcast.

222
00:14:07,501 --> 00:14:09,375
Yeah. After saving
all our asses.

223
00:14:09,376 --> 00:14:11,084
No.
I'm sorry,

224
00:14:11,085 --> 00:14:13,167
but by the <i>tulkun</i> way,
he bears the deaths.

225
00:14:13,168 --> 00:14:14,167
[Payakan rumbling]

226
00:14:14,168 --> 00:14:15,585
All those
who died in the battle.

227
00:14:16,501 --> 00:14:17,876
He bears those deaths.

228
00:14:20,043 --> 00:14:22,835
I'm sorry. You saved us all.

229
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:24,835
[rumbling]

230
00:14:29,501 --> 00:14:31,334
[distorted] Forever, Brother.

231
00:14:31,335 --> 00:14:32,417
[normal] Always.

232
00:14:32,418 --> 00:14:34,210
[bellows]

233
00:14:38,126 --> 00:14:41,085
[exo-pack beeping]

234
00:14:41,918 --> 00:14:43,751
[gasping, choking]

235
00:14:45,376 --> 00:14:46,376
Dad!

236
00:14:50,585 --> 00:14:52,334
- Wait, where's the spare?
- It's in the basket, I think.

237
00:14:52,335 --> 00:14:53,667
Hey! Wake up! Where is it?

238
00:14:53,668 --> 00:14:55,542
- Hey! Where's the spare mask?
- What?

239
00:14:55,543 --> 00:14:57,292
Where's the spare mask?
Used to be there. Where is it?

240
00:14:57,293 --> 00:14:58,709
- I don't know.
- Find it.

241
00:14:58,710 --> 00:15:00,542
- It's not here.
- Speak to me. Where is it?

242
00:15:00,543 --> 00:15:02,625
- [Kiri] I can't find it.
- [Jake] Hey, hey! Where is it?

243
00:15:02,626 --> 00:15:04,043
- Come on. Come on. Come on.
- I got it. Dad.

244
00:15:04,585 --> 00:15:06,210
- Dad. I found it.
- Hurry.

245
00:15:08,543 --> 00:15:09,959
[beeping stops]

246
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:11,417
- [breathing heavily]
- [air hisses]

247
00:15:11,418 --> 00:15:13,209
Spider, no.

248
00:15:13,210 --> 00:15:14,292
Breathe.

249
00:15:14,293 --> 00:15:16,292
- Breathe.
- Breathe.

250
00:15:16,293 --> 00:15:17,668
[Jake] Deep and slow.

251
00:15:18,335 --> 00:15:19,501
Deep and slow.

252
00:15:20,001 --> 00:15:21,417
There you go.
You're okay.

253
00:15:21,418 --> 00:15:24,543
[breathing deeply] I'm good.
I'm good. I'm okay.

254
00:15:26,710 --> 00:15:28,835
<i>Skxawng.</i>
You have to be careful.

255
00:15:29,376 --> 00:15:31,000
- Careful's my middle name.
- Yeah, <i>skxawng.</i>

256
00:15:31,001 --> 00:15:32,542
You should be more careful,
little baby.

257
00:15:32,543 --> 00:15:33,625
Pay attention.

258
00:15:33,626 --> 00:15:36,417
- Get off. Get off. Get off.
- Stupid is your middle name.

259
00:15:36,418 --> 00:15:37,500
- Be careful, little baby.
- No, let him go.

260
00:15:37,501 --> 00:15:39,584
- You have to pay attention.
<i>- Skxawng</i> is his middle name.

261
00:15:39,585 --> 00:15:41,834
- Are you sure you're okay?
- Yeah, I feel fine.

262
00:15:41,835 --> 00:15:43,085
[horn blowing]

263
00:15:44,001 --> 00:15:45,125
[Tsireya] The Windtraders.

264
00:15:45,126 --> 00:15:46,918
- The Windtraders are here.
- [Na'vi cheering]

265
00:15:48,543 --> 00:15:49,750
The Windtraders
are coming.

266
00:15:49,751 --> 00:15:50,834
Come on!

267
00:15:50,835 --> 00:15:51,960
Come on. Let's go.

268
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:53,668
- [Tsireya] Come on.
- [Tuk laughs]

269
00:15:54,626 --> 00:15:55,750
Come on, Tuk.

270
00:15:55,751 --> 00:15:58,251
[♪ joyful music plays]

271
00:15:59,543 --> 00:16:01,168
[Lo'ak] Whoo!

272
00:16:05,210 --> 00:16:06,210
[whoops]

273
00:16:14,168 --> 00:16:15,626
[whoops]

274
00:16:18,085 --> 00:16:20,376
Hey! [whooping]

275
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:31,335
[Na'vi chattering,
playing music]

276
00:16:35,710 --> 00:16:36,710
Tsireya.

277
00:16:37,543 --> 00:16:38,918
[gasps]

278
00:16:40,376 --> 00:16:42,084
Look. [chuckles]

279
00:16:42,085 --> 00:16:43,709
Look at him.

280
00:16:43,710 --> 00:16:45,293
He's not going
to take up much room.

281
00:16:46,001 --> 00:16:47,501
As long as he's no trouble.

282
00:16:48,501 --> 00:16:50,375
- Take a knee. Let's go. Tuk.
- Kiri.

283
00:16:50,376 --> 00:16:51,834
- Come on, Kiri.
- What?

284
00:16:51,835 --> 00:16:53,709
- Kiri, please.
- Children, please sit down.

285
00:16:53,710 --> 00:16:54,751
[Jake] Please, sit.

286
00:16:56,251 --> 00:16:59,001
Your mother and I have
come to a decision.

287
00:17:02,376 --> 00:17:04,084
[sighs]

288
00:17:04,085 --> 00:17:06,084
Spider, you're going to live
back in High Camp with Norm.

289
00:17:06,085 --> 00:17:07,834
- What?
- The Windtraders will take you.

290
00:17:07,835 --> 00:17:09,875
- No, Dad.
- No, Dad. He can't.

291
00:17:09,876 --> 00:17:12,375
Spider, you can't live
in a mask

292
00:17:12,376 --> 00:17:13,459
day and night.

293
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:15,375
I just want
to stay here with you.

294
00:17:15,376 --> 00:17:18,085
- I know, but it's too risky.
- This isn't fair.

295
00:17:18,918 --> 00:17:21,084
Please. You're the only family
I've ever known.

296
00:17:21,085 --> 00:17:22,584
[Jake] This is what's
best for you.

297
00:17:22,585 --> 00:17:24,334
But, Dad,
he's our best friend.

298
00:17:24,335 --> 00:17:25,709
Can't we just
find a way?

299
00:17:25,710 --> 00:17:26,792
[Jake] It's too dangerous.

300
00:17:26,793 --> 00:17:29,125
You're one dead battery away
from being dead yourself.

301
00:17:29,126 --> 00:17:31,292
He belongs
with his own kind.

302
00:17:31,293 --> 00:17:32,126
Mom.

303
00:17:32,751 --> 00:17:35,834
And what kind
is that, Mother? Alien?

304
00:17:35,835 --> 00:17:37,209
- Kiri.
- Pink-ass.

305
00:17:37,210 --> 00:17:38,292
- Kiri.
- Stop.

306
00:17:38,293 --> 00:17:40,751
You hate them so much,
that's all you see.

307
00:17:41,585 --> 00:17:42,585
It's Spider.

308
00:17:43,460 --> 00:17:44,750
Please, Jake.

309
00:17:44,751 --> 00:17:46,917
Mr. Sully, I won't be
any problem. You know that.

310
00:17:46,918 --> 00:17:48,125
Dad, this isn't right.

311
00:17:48,126 --> 00:17:50,334
Spider is part of this family.

312
00:17:50,335 --> 00:17:51,834
He will never

313
00:17:51,835 --> 00:17:53,793
- be a part of this family.
- Mother, no.

314
00:17:54,460 --> 00:17:55,668
[Kiri sobs]

315
00:17:56,168 --> 00:17:59,000
The caravan is the safest way
to move him.

316
00:17:59,001 --> 00:18:00,542
- No, please.
- He's going today.

317
00:18:00,543 --> 00:18:02,584
- You can't do this. Dad, he's--
- It's a done deal.

318
00:18:02,585 --> 00:18:06,084
Enough! This is a family.
It's not a democracy.

319
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:07,292
All right?

320
00:18:07,293 --> 00:18:08,375
I hate you!

321
00:18:08,376 --> 00:18:09,584
This is what is best,
baby girl.

322
00:18:09,585 --> 00:18:10,667
- No!
- Hey, it's okay.

323
00:18:10,668 --> 00:18:12,001
Don't touch me!

324
00:18:12,751 --> 00:18:14,293
- Hey. It's okay.
- [sobs]

325
00:18:15,710 --> 00:18:16,960
- [Jake] You understand?
- No.

326
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:20,043
I already lost my brother.

327
00:18:20,751 --> 00:18:22,251
I can't lose anyone else.

328
00:18:24,168 --> 00:18:25,168
[hisses]

329
00:18:28,835 --> 00:18:30,584
[Lo'ak] <i>Sullys stick together.</i>

330
00:18:30,585 --> 00:18:32,209
[Jake sighs]

331
00:18:32,210 --> 00:18:34,418
[Lo'ak] <i>Yep, that's
the family motto.</i>

332
00:18:38,335 --> 00:18:40,000
- It's bullshit.
- This isn't fair.

333
00:18:40,001 --> 00:18:41,709
[Jake] Okay, okay.

334
00:18:41,710 --> 00:18:43,542
Hey. All right.
How about this?

335
00:18:43,543 --> 00:18:45,709
We all go together
to drop him off.

336
00:18:45,710 --> 00:18:46,543
Kiri.

337
00:18:48,251 --> 00:18:50,250
You said you wanted to see
your grandmother.

338
00:18:50,251 --> 00:18:53,835
Yeah, it will be an adventure.
For the whole family.

339
00:18:58,418 --> 00:19:00,126
Yeah. Cool.

340
00:19:03,168 --> 00:19:04,626
[shrieks]

341
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,126
[Jake] Hey, stay here.

342
00:19:16,793 --> 00:19:20,334
Our arrangement was
for the pink-skinned boy only.

343
00:19:20,335 --> 00:19:21,959
We won't be any trouble.

344
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:23,417
You are already trouble.

345
00:19:23,418 --> 00:19:25,500
A trader must move freely.

346
00:19:25,501 --> 00:19:26,501
We cannot choose sides.

347
00:19:27,335 --> 00:19:29,167
Having <i>Toruk Makto</i>
on board

348
00:19:29,168 --> 00:19:32,376
cuts very close to
choosing a side in this war.

349
00:19:33,001 --> 00:19:34,750
Yeah, but you're mistaken.

350
00:19:34,751 --> 00:19:36,835
<i>Toruk Makto</i>
was never on your ship.

351
00:19:39,626 --> 00:19:41,793
But if he was ever
aboard, then...

352
00:19:43,043 --> 00:19:45,792
him and his woman would be
happy to fly as outriders

353
00:19:45,793 --> 00:19:47,210
and protect your caravan.

354
00:19:50,251 --> 00:19:51,376
Perhaps so.

355
00:19:52,335 --> 00:19:54,626
The <i>Mangkwan</i> raiders
grow more aggressive.

356
00:19:55,126 --> 00:19:56,126
[Jake] Hmm.

357
00:19:56,793 --> 00:19:58,668
Very well.
I meet you on this.

358
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:02,168
[sighs]

359
00:20:02,793 --> 00:20:05,334
- [horn blowing]
- [♪ adventurous music plays]

360
00:20:05,335 --> 00:20:06,710
Cast off!

361
00:20:08,001 --> 00:20:09,125
Come on.

362
00:20:09,126 --> 00:20:10,418
Cast off!

363
00:20:12,585 --> 00:20:14,251
Cast off below!

364
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:18,876
[♪ singing in Na'vi]

365
00:20:19,751 --> 00:20:21,875
Lo'ak! [chuckles] Lo'ak!

366
00:20:21,876 --> 00:20:23,418
Oh, Tsireya!
Tsireya!

367
00:20:23,918 --> 00:20:24,751
Lo'ak! [chuckles]

368
00:20:26,168 --> 00:20:27,501
Ready about!

369
00:20:28,918 --> 00:20:31,500
[crew member 1]
Ready about! On all lines.

370
00:20:31,501 --> 00:20:33,001
[Peylak] Bow to starboard.

371
00:20:40,543 --> 00:20:42,959
Windward vanes out full!

372
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:45,250
Haul out and raise
full to windward!

373
00:20:45,251 --> 00:20:46,376
[crew members] Heave!

374
00:20:46,960 --> 00:20:49,710
Heave!

375
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:53,751
Heave!

376
00:20:56,001 --> 00:20:58,251
Lighten ship. Come up easy.

377
00:21:05,876 --> 00:21:07,418
Windward out full!

378
00:21:08,876 --> 00:21:10,835
[chuckles]

379
00:21:11,335 --> 00:21:13,835
Make all and set taut!

380
00:21:51,001 --> 00:21:54,792
[♪ Windtraders
singing in Na'vi]

381
00:21:54,793 --> 00:21:56,210
Whoo! Yeah!

382
00:22:03,376 --> 00:22:05,251
[Lo'ak] <i>Everyone mourns
in their own way.</i>

383
00:22:09,251 --> 00:22:10,418
<i>For me,</i>

384
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,251
<i>it's being up here alone.</i>

385
00:22:15,126 --> 00:22:16,876
<i>I feel him with me.</i>

386
00:22:19,376 --> 00:22:20,501
Bro, check it out.

387
00:22:21,126 --> 00:22:23,418
[Lo'ak] <i>I hear his voice
in the wind.</i>

388
00:22:24,960 --> 00:22:26,460
[ululates]

389
00:22:35,418 --> 00:22:36,750
[squawks]

390
00:22:36,751 --> 00:22:37,876
[Jake sighs]

391
00:22:39,585 --> 00:22:40,585
Hold this.

392
00:22:50,335 --> 00:22:52,334
- Hey, Dad, I've been thinking.
- Yeah?

393
00:22:52,335 --> 00:22:53,834
I should carry a rifle.

394
00:22:53,835 --> 00:22:55,250
And I could fly with you.

395
00:22:55,251 --> 00:22:56,251
Yeah.

396
00:22:57,085 --> 00:22:58,584
That's gonna happen. [grunts]

397
00:22:58,585 --> 00:23:00,125
Why not?

398
00:23:00,126 --> 00:23:01,709
You trained me to shoot, okay?

399
00:23:01,710 --> 00:23:03,210
I know what I'm doing.

400
00:23:03,751 --> 00:23:05,292
Yeah? Where's your comms?

401
00:23:05,293 --> 00:23:06,710
I called you like five times.

402
00:23:08,376 --> 00:23:10,001
Wear your comms.

403
00:23:10,710 --> 00:23:11,710
That's rule number one.

404
00:23:13,668 --> 00:23:15,001
You can't even do that.

405
00:23:21,251 --> 00:23:22,501
[groans]

406
00:23:27,210 --> 00:23:28,335
[Wainfleet]
Bring up the next one.

407
00:23:30,376 --> 00:23:31,376
That's it.

408
00:23:34,001 --> 00:23:35,167
What you got?

409
00:23:35,168 --> 00:23:36,709
So, I promised this guy
on imaging

410
00:23:36,710 --> 00:23:38,376
a case of beer if he
ever got something for us.

411
00:23:39,751 --> 00:23:41,042
Long-range patrols
clocked these guys

412
00:23:41,043 --> 00:23:42,834
when they punched
our airspace.

413
00:23:42,835 --> 00:23:44,043
A routine flyby.

414
00:23:44,793 --> 00:23:46,001
Here's the enhanced.

415
00:23:50,460 --> 00:23:51,668
Smile, bitches.

416
00:23:53,626 --> 00:23:56,375
- When? [clicks tongue]
- 1350 today.

417
00:23:56,376 --> 00:23:57,459
I got coordinates.

418
00:23:57,460 --> 00:23:58,710
Let's mount up.

419
00:24:00,043 --> 00:24:01,085
Thank you.

420
00:24:09,710 --> 00:24:12,001
[horn blowing]

421
00:24:15,876 --> 00:24:19,501
Haul in hard!

422
00:24:27,210 --> 00:24:28,793
Steady on course.

423
00:24:31,168 --> 00:24:33,168
[exo-pack beeping]

424
00:24:34,043 --> 00:24:35,125
[beeping stops]

425
00:24:35,126 --> 00:24:36,126
Your pack.

426
00:24:36,668 --> 00:24:38,251
I'm good.
I got plenty of time.

427
00:24:49,793 --> 00:24:50,793
Clear ahead.

428
00:25:06,793 --> 00:25:08,000
Jake!

429
00:25:08,001 --> 00:25:09,375
<i>Mangkwan!</i>

430
00:25:09,376 --> 00:25:10,792
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

431
00:25:10,793 --> 00:25:11,917
<i>Mangkwan</i> raiders.
Weapons up.

432
00:25:11,918 --> 00:25:13,001
Sound the alarm!

433
00:25:14,543 --> 00:25:15,668
[shouts]

434
00:25:18,626 --> 00:25:19,542
[ululating]

435
00:25:19,543 --> 00:25:21,167
- [Jake] Weapons up!
- Kiri, go.

436
00:25:21,168 --> 00:25:22,459
- Run!
- Go.

437
00:25:22,460 --> 00:25:23,750
Get these out.

438
00:25:23,751 --> 00:25:25,126
Come on, let's go.
Let's go. To cover.

439
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:28,168
[grunts]

440
00:25:28,793 --> 00:25:29,793
[shouts]

441
00:25:30,793 --> 00:25:32,126
[shrieks]

442
00:25:34,626 --> 00:25:35,501
[grunts]

443
00:25:36,168 --> 00:25:37,167
Go, go.

444
00:25:37,168 --> 00:25:38,875
Protect your sisters.
Can you do that?

445
00:25:38,876 --> 00:25:40,710
Yes, sir.
Stay under cover.

446
00:25:42,710 --> 00:25:43,792
[crew member]
Repel boarders!

447
00:25:43,793 --> 00:25:45,668
[Jake shouts]

448
00:25:49,043 --> 00:25:50,460
[shouts]

449
00:25:57,793 --> 00:25:59,501
[panting]

450
00:26:03,001 --> 00:26:04,418
[shrieks]

451
00:26:09,210 --> 00:26:10,501
Spider, here.

452
00:26:14,460 --> 00:26:15,543
Shit, my comms.

453
00:26:24,376 --> 00:26:25,292
[grunts]

454
00:26:25,293 --> 00:26:27,668
- [grunting]
- [groans]

455
00:26:28,668 --> 00:26:29,834
Stay with the girls. [coughs]

456
00:26:29,835 --> 00:26:30,710
Bro,
where are you going?

457
00:26:34,668 --> 00:26:36,043
Bro, you're supposed
to stay here.

458
00:26:36,918 --> 00:26:38,085
[shrieks]

459
00:26:43,418 --> 00:26:44,460
[grunts]

460
00:26:45,376 --> 00:26:46,210
[shrieks]

461
00:26:48,710 --> 00:26:49,876
[shrieks]

462
00:26:52,126 --> 00:26:53,126
[shouts]

463
00:26:53,793 --> 00:26:55,043
- [grunts]
- [shrieks]

464
00:26:59,251 --> 00:27:00,917
- [grunts]
- [shrieks]

465
00:27:00,918 --> 00:27:01,960
[shouts]

466
00:27:04,043 --> 00:27:05,043
Come on.

467
00:27:06,751 --> 00:27:07,793
Release.

468
00:27:09,460 --> 00:27:10,959
[grunting]

469
00:27:10,960 --> 00:27:13,209
- [grunts]
- [shrieks]

470
00:27:13,210 --> 00:27:14,750
[pants]

471
00:27:14,751 --> 00:27:16,167
[shrieks]

472
00:27:16,168 --> 00:27:17,917
[breathing heavily]

473
00:27:17,918 --> 00:27:19,292
[ululates]

474
00:27:19,293 --> 00:27:20,500
[Spider] Get back.

475
00:27:20,501 --> 00:27:21,543
- Get back.
- [gasps]

476
00:27:24,710 --> 00:27:25,710
[shouts]

477
00:27:26,460 --> 00:27:28,334
- [grunts]
- [grunts]

478
00:27:28,335 --> 00:27:30,167
[groaning]

479
00:27:30,168 --> 00:27:32,460
- [shouts]
- [grunting]

480
00:27:34,501 --> 00:27:35,626
[groans]

481
00:27:36,418 --> 00:27:37,417
[shouts]

482
00:27:37,418 --> 00:27:38,710
[grunting]

483
00:27:39,293 --> 00:27:40,793
[both grunting]

484
00:27:41,293 --> 00:27:42,668
[panting]

485
00:27:53,626 --> 00:27:54,709
[grunts, shouts]

486
00:27:54,710 --> 00:27:55,793
[grunts]

487
00:27:57,751 --> 00:27:58,668
[shrieks]

488
00:28:04,460 --> 00:28:05,960
[grunts, exhales sharply]

489
00:28:06,918 --> 00:28:07,751
[shouts]

490
00:28:08,876 --> 00:28:09,959
I am

491
00:28:09,960 --> 00:28:11,251
the fire!

492
00:28:11,835 --> 00:28:14,168
[shouting]

493
00:28:15,043 --> 00:28:16,460
[snarls]

494
00:28:23,376 --> 00:28:25,209
[shouts]

495
00:28:25,210 --> 00:28:26,418
[grunts]

496
00:28:28,793 --> 00:28:30,167
[shouting]

497
00:28:30,168 --> 00:28:31,168
Oh, sh...

498
00:28:33,460 --> 00:28:34,460
[grunts]

499
00:28:35,751 --> 00:28:36,751
Hey!

500
00:28:37,293 --> 00:28:38,293
[groans]

501
00:28:39,085 --> 00:28:40,334
[shouts]

502
00:28:40,335 --> 00:28:41,460
[grunts]

503
00:28:47,043 --> 00:28:49,792
[shouts]

504
00:28:49,793 --> 00:28:51,668
[groans]

505
00:28:53,085 --> 00:28:54,085
[shouts]

506
00:28:55,418 --> 00:28:57,001
[groans, shouts]

507
00:29:00,126 --> 00:29:01,460
[shrieks]

508
00:29:05,126 --> 00:29:06,835
[both grunting]

509
00:29:09,543 --> 00:29:10,793
[grunts, shouts]

510
00:29:11,710 --> 00:29:13,043
- [shouts]
- [grunts]

511
00:29:14,251 --> 00:29:15,543
- [Kiri] Tuk.
- Go. Go.

512
00:29:16,376 --> 00:29:17,792
Climb. Climb.

513
00:29:17,793 --> 00:29:19,251
Get up. Hurry.

514
00:29:21,001 --> 00:29:22,043
[exclaims]

515
00:29:22,710 --> 00:29:23,876
[shrieks]

516
00:29:25,835 --> 00:29:27,709
[groans] Spider,
grab on.

517
00:29:27,710 --> 00:29:28,792
Come on, let's go.

518
00:29:28,793 --> 00:29:29,710
Hold on.

519
00:29:34,960 --> 00:29:35,876
[grunts]

520
00:29:36,751 --> 00:29:37,667
[grunts]

521
00:29:37,668 --> 00:29:39,210
[♪ dramatic music plays]

522
00:29:42,668 --> 00:29:43,625
[scoffs]

523
00:29:43,626 --> 00:29:45,376
[gasping]

524
00:29:57,043 --> 00:29:58,876
Neytiri, Neytiri,
do you copy?

525
00:30:01,751 --> 00:30:03,626
[screeching]

526
00:30:06,793 --> 00:30:07,835
Crap, crap, crap,
crap, crap.

527
00:30:09,585 --> 00:30:10,792
- Guys, it's Lo'ak.
- Where?

528
00:30:10,793 --> 00:30:12,710
Come on.
We gotta get him. Go. Go.

529
00:30:14,126 --> 00:30:15,459
Lo'ak.

530
00:30:15,460 --> 00:30:16,834
